# Playwright constitution

Short guardrails for specs, POMs, and QA automation in this repo.

| MUST | |
|------|---|
| Locators | Role-first in POMs (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByText`); no inline locators in specs |
| Assertions | Web-first `expect` in tests only — never in `pages/` |
| Auth | Reuse `storageState` / project fixtures; no per-test login unless the plan requires it |
| Data | Unique names (Faker or suffixes); clean up what you create (see **api-cleanup** skill) |
| Tags | Exactly one tag per test (`@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, `@e2e`, `@destructive`) — not on `describe` |

| SHOULD | |
|--------|---|
| Factories | Faker (or shared helpers) for entities and form fields |
| Enums | Shared constants for labels, routes, and API paths used more than once |
| POM docs | JSDoc on public action methods when intent is not obvious from the name |

| WON'T | |
|-------|---|
| XPath | No XPath locators |
| Sleeps | No `waitForTimeout`; use auto-waiting, `expect`, or event-driven waits |
| Secrets | No hardcoded credentials or tokens in repo — env / CI secrets only |
| Types | No `any` in new test code |
| Assertions | No weakening, deleting, or commenting out `expect` to go green |
| Healing | No locator “heal” when triage says **real app bug** — file the bug instead |
| Tags | No tags on `test.describe` blocks |

## Agent governance

Behavioral contract for agents in this repo — not enforced by hooks; follow it on every non-trivial task.

### Audit-then-edit

Inspect the repo, docs, and runtime context **before** changing files. Proposals come first; edits come after the confidence gate allows them.

### Proposal (required before edit)

For any non-trivial task, emit a **Proposal** block before editing:

| Field | Content |
|-------|---------|
| **Scope** | What will change, and what is explicitly out of scope |
| **Confidence** | Integer 1–10 |
| **Rationale** | Why this approach fits the codebase and the request |
| **Unknowns** | Gaps that could change the plan (missing creds, unclear product behavior, unverified paths) |

Trivial work (typos, single-line fixes obviously requested, pure Q&A with no repo edits) may skip the Proposal.

### Confidence gate

| Confidence | Action |
|------------|--------|
| **< 5** | Do **not** proceed with edits. Ask for the missing input or run targeted exploration first. |
| **5–7** | Proceed only if **Unknowns** are stated explicitly and the human approves the Proposal. |
| **≥ 8** | Proceed with the plan; still list material Unknowns when they exist. |

### No invention

Never guess or fabricate paths, enum values, env var names, credentials, API messages, or Jira keys. **Ask** the human or **explore** the repo, MCP, and docs until the fact is verified.

